# Marketing deploy smoke (from 2026-10-22)

**Baseline date:** 22 Oct 2026. New Sheetomatic production deploys must pass this smoke after Ready — do not call the ship done until HTTP checks pass on the **new** `dpl=` id.

## Why this exists

- FMS dual videos (`PM8E3mCw67Q` + `acTJOocmuZM`) lived on an unmerged branch and were never on `main`, so a “correct” main deploy showed **zero** videos on `/services/flow`.
- Field Executive was moved to peer slug `/services/field-tracking` and renamed; looking under HR made it look “missing”.
- Production aliases can stick on an older Ready deploy after a failed tip build — always verify live `dpl=`, not dashboard lore.

## Must stay on main

| Surface | Requirement |
|---------|-------------|
| `/services/flow` | Two-video compare: sheet FMS `PM8E3mCw67Q` + AI FMS `acTJOocmuZM` in `services-category-content.tsx` (`.fms-video-compare`) |
| `/services/field-tracking` | **200** — Field Executive Management Systems peer page |
| Services hub / browse | Card label **Field Executive Management Systems** → `/services/field-tracking` |

Do **not** put FMS embeds only in unused `service-detail-content.tsx` — live route is `ServicesCategoryContent`.

## Pre-ship checklist (release-ops)

After production Ready on **sheetomatic-redesign**, run:

```bash
npm run deploy:verify
```

That script enforces forward-only baseline + field-tracking 200 + FMS dual video markers + legacy HR field redirect. Exit 0 required.

If live `dpl=` is still old: re-alias / promote the **new** Ready tip on **sheetomatic-redesign** only — never Instant Rollback behind the baseline, never attach domains to `sheetomatic-redesign-deploy-v2`.

## Do not

- Merge marketing branches that skip the FMS compare block.
- Filter Field Executive out of the **top-level** services browse list.
- Treat a green GitHub check on deploy-v2 (no `DATABASE_URL`) as production proof.
- Restore unused `service-detail-content.tsx` as the FMS video host.
